        "geology": "Sandstone and quartzite with intermittent shale bands of Table Mountain Group, underlain by Cape granite",
        "hydrology": "Jonkershoek valley falls in a predominantly winter rainfall (April to September) regime with 75 % of annual rain falling in this period. Streamflow has been measured from 6 catchments in the valley from 1938",
        "soils": "Mixed colluvial soils with major forms being Hutton, Magwa and Nomanci.  They are acid sandy loams, low in organic matter and phosphorus. Soils have high infiltration capacity and are well-drained",
        "vegetation": "The site is predominantly fire-prone mountain fynbos. Riparian zones and screes are dominated by afrotemperate forest"
      },
